# Keep these OFF the live site entirely.
#
# Vercel serves any deployed file straight from its CDN, before the app runs — so the file
# allowlist in server.js, which works locally, does nothing in production. Checked, not assumed:
# CLAUDE.md and SESSION-HANDOFF.md both came back in full from the live site.
#
# Nothing here is needed to answer a request, so leaving it out costs nothing and stops the
# business notes, the workflow plans and the internal scripts being downloadable by anyone who
# guesses a filename.
#
# The application source (server.js, routes/, utils/, storage/) still has to be deployed, so it
# is still readable. That needs Vercel to stop treating the repo root as a static site, which is
# a bigger change than this one.

*.md
tests/
tools/
prototypes/
apps-script/
lambda/
.claude/
NEW-FLOW-CHART.html
jest.config.js
.env*
